= Bit (technical) =

== Formal definitions ==
A binary digit is an element of an alphabet of cardinality two. A bit as a logarithmic information unit is defined by using logarithms to base 2. Thus, a symbol's representational alphabet size and its statistical information are separate variables.

<pre>
Hartley (equiprobable): H_0 = log_2(N) bits
Self-information:       I(x) = -log_2 p(x) bits
Shannon entropy:        H(X) = -sum_x p(x) log_2 p(x) bits
Convention:             0 log_2(0) = 0
Conditional entropy:    H(X|Y) = -sum_{x,y} p(x,y) log_2 p(x|y)
Mutual information:     I(X;Y) = H(X) - H(X|Y)
                      = sum_{x,y} p(x,y) log_2[p(x,y)/(p(x)p(y))]
</pre>

All entropy sums refer to a specified probability distribution. A rare realization can have self-information above one bit even if the source alphabet has two symbols; for example p(x)=0.1 gives I(x)=3.3219 bits, although the binary source's maximum ''average entropy'' is one bit. An ideal n-bit binary string alphabet has 2^n possibilities. Actual coding rates depend on the source, channel, coding constraints and errors.

== Worked probability examples ==
For Bernoulli(p):
<pre>
h_2(p) = -p log_2(p) - (1-p) log_2(1-p)
h_2(0.5) = 1 bit
h_2(1) = 0 bits
h_2(0.9) = 0.4689955936 bits
H(uniform 8 outcomes) = log_2 8 = 3 bits
</pre>

If X is a fair binary variable and Y=X without noise, H(X|Y)=0 and I(X;Y)=1 bit. If X and Y are independent fair binary variables, I(X;Y)=0 even though H(X)=H(Y)=1. Statistical mutual information alone does not entail semantic agreement or causal influence.

== Physical and conceptual boundaries ==
* '''Representation vs entropy:''' allocating one storage cell per binary symbol does not make a deterministic recorded sequence statistically random.
* '''Thermodynamics:''' for unbiased memory erasure under the idealized Landauer setup, heat dissipated to a bath at temperature T is bounded by k_B T ln(2); erasure is a many-to-one logical operation. The bound does not assert that every reversible logic operation dissipates this amount.
* '''Quantum:''' the qubit state a|0> + b|1> has complex amplitudes with |a|^2+|b|^2=1. Accessible classical information from a qubit alone is constrained; a single qubit is not automatically a two-classical-bit message.
* '''Biology:''' sequence entropy is defined over a modeled ensemble of sequences/positions; neural spike-train information depends on response and stimulus models, recording resolution and sampling.
* '''Semantics:''' Shannon measures quantify statistical choice structure, not meaning, truth, intention, or ontology.

